    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1333">

                <pb facs="1592" n="1394" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv02/pg1394"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Department of the Army Files</note>
                <head>No. 1333<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The President
                        to the Chief of Staff, United States Army</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Marshall</hi>)<anchor n="1" xml:id="d1333-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Babelsberg</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-07-27">July 27, 1945</date>.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Replying to your request for information in regard to the tripartite agreement
                    that “troops of the three powers should be withdrawn from Teheran at once”, you
                    are informed that it is my desire that United States troops be withdrawn from
                    Teheran within 60 days if it is practicable to do so.</p>
                <p>It is not intended that the Ridley and
                        Schwarzkopf missions and that
                        A. T. C. personnel and facilities in Iran be
                    withdrawn at the present time.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1333-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d1333-f1-content">
                <p>Printed from the text relayed by Hull to
                    the War Department in telegram No. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Victory</hi> 370 of
                    July 27, where it is described as a “memorandum for General Marshall signed by the President
                    under date July 27”.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
